214.
Obligations of information utility.
- For the purposes of providing core services to any person, every information utility shall-
(a)
create and store financial information in a universally accessible format;
(b)
accept electronic submissions of financial information from persons who are under obligations to submit financial
information under sub-section (1) of section 215, in such form and manner as may be specified by regulations;
(c)
accept, in specified form and manner, electronic submissions of financial information from persons who intend to submit
such information;
(d)
